{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blues Came Callin' feels like a natural next choice because I want blues guitar, which connects directly with my interest in Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels.",
    "Revelator appeals to me because its blues and roots sound fits the part of my recent listening I want to explore further."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Chicago's horn-driven pop rock and The Smile Sessions' elaborate vocal pop do not offer the blues guitar and vocals I want right now.",
    "ANASTASIS feels too atmospheric for this visit, while the Eagles and Steely Dan collections feel like larger commitments than I want to make."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some classic rock seems to have been treated as interest in a broad range of classic rock, even though the sound matters more to me than that shared association.",
    "Interest in familiar musicians seems to have been stretched into interest in extensive collections, which I would pass over today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The blues guitar connection between Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels matters more to my current choice than a general rock connection.",
    "I rarely choose something unless it feels closely relevant, so a focused blues or roots album gives me more reason to act than a loosely related recommendation."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in rock but only partly capture my current preference for blues guitar, vocals, and roots music."
}"}
